  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It's a sunny day.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You do not use an umbrella.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A\u21d2B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\u00acA\u21d2\u00acB.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $\u00acA:$ It's not a sunny day.\n\n- $\u00acB:$ You use an umbrella.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it's not a sunny day, then you use an umbrella.",
